# Release Readiness Checklist

A structured checklist to ensure all critical steps are completed before, during, and after a release. Adapt this to fit your team’s workflow and tooling.

---

## 1. Planning & Scope Confirmation
- [ ] Requirements finalized and documented  
- [ ] Release scope approved by product/engineering  
- [ ] Dependencies identified and communicated  
- [ ] Risk areas flagged early  
- [ ] Stakeholder list updated  

---

## 2. Environment & Build Preparation
- [ ] Build pipeline validated  
- [ ] Environments stable and accessible  
- [ ] Feature flags reviewed  
- [ ] Configuration changes documented  
- [ ] Deployment steps confirmed  

---

## 3. Testing & Validation
- [ ] QA test cases executed  
- [ ] Regression testing completed  
- [ ] UAT sign-off received  
- [ ] Performance checks completed  
- [ ] Bugs triaged and prioritized  

---

## 4. Communication & Coordination
- [ ] Release timeline shared with all stakeholders  
- [ ] Go/no-go meeting scheduled  
- [ ] Support teams notified  
- [ ] Release notes drafted  
- [ ] Customer-facing messaging prepared (if applicable)  

---

## 5. Deployment Readiness
- [ ] Deployment owner assigned  
- [ ] Rollback plan documented  
- [ ] Monitoring tools configured  
- [ ] Access permissions validated  
- [ ] Final go/no-go decision recorded  

---

## 6. Post-Release Activities
- [ ] Smoke tests completed  
- [ ] Monitoring dashboards reviewed  
- [ ] Issues logged and assigned  
- [ ] Release notes published  
- [ ] Retrospective scheduled  

